# The pointer, the camera and the undo history of E8.1.4 in one flow, with no front end: select by click, move by drag, marquee,
# resize by a handle, a drop above a sibling that reorders, a pan and a zoom to the pointer, and then every undo step back to the
# start. The pointer points are screen points; the camera is at its home until the pan, so they are world points until then.
#
# The file (flow.json): `f` is a column at (0, 0), 200 by 300, with `a` (10 to 30), `b` (35 to 65) and `c` (70 to 110) in it, all at
# x 10 and 50 wide; `g` is a free frame at (400, 0) with the rectangle `fg` at its own (20, 20), 30 by 30: world (420, 20).
open flow.json
camera viewport 800 600
# A drop in a flow needs the laid-out canvas: the harness starts with it off.
palette auto layout run auto-layout
expect clean
expect state /history/undoSteps 0

# 1. Select by click. Hover first, then the press selects at once, and a click is not an edit.
pointer move 435 35
expect state /pointer/hover "fg"
pointer down 435 35
expect state /selection ["fg"]
pointer up 435 35
expect state /pointer/gesture {"type":"idle"}
expect state /history/undoSteps 0
expect state /confirmedSeq 0

# 2. Move by drag: nothing is written while the pointer is down, one op when it is let go, one undo step.
pointer down 435 35
pointer move 440 40
pointer move 445 45
expect state /pointer/gesture/type "move"
expect preview /kind "move"
expect preview /dx 10
expect preview /dy 10
expect node fg x 20
expect node fg y 20
expect state /history/undoSteps 0
expect state /confirmedSeq 0
pointer up 445 45
expect clean
expect preview /kind null
expect node fg x 30
expect node fg y 30
expect state /history/undoSteps 1
expect state /confirmedSeq 1

# 3. Marquee: a press on empty canvas starts a rubber band, a normalised rectangle in world space, and the selection stays as it
# was until the release; then the frame the band overlaps is selected, not the three rectangles inside it. A selection is not an edit.
pointer down 250 150
pointer move 100 50
expect state /selection ["fg"]
expect preview /kind "marquee"
expect preview /rect/x 100
expect preview /rect/y 50
expect preview /rect/w 150
expect preview /rect/h 100
pointer move -50 -50
pointer up -50 -50
expect state /selection ["f"]
expect state /history/undoSteps 1

# 4. Resize by a handle. `fg` is now drawn at world (430, 30), 30 by 30, so its south east handle is at (460, 60).
pointer down 445 45
pointer up 445 45
expect state /selection ["fg"]
pointer move 460 60
expect state /pointer/cursor "nwse-resize"
pointer down 460 60
expect state /selection ["fg"]
pointer move 465 67
expect preview /kind "resize"
expect preview /world/w 35
expect preview /world/h 37
expect node fg w 30
expect node fg h 30
expect state /history/undoSteps 1
pointer up 465 67
expect clean
expect node fg x 30
expect node fg y 30
expect node fg w 35
expect node fg h 37
expect state /history/undoSteps 2
expect state /confirmedSeq 2

# 5. A drop above a sibling reorders. `b` is drawn at y 35 to 65; the pointer goes above the middle of `a`. Until the release the
# preview is the insertion line in `f` at index 0 and the file is as it was.
pointer down 30 50
expect state /selection ["b"]
pointer move 30 40
pointer move 30 15
expect state /pointer/gesture/type "move"
expect preview /kind "move"
expect preview /slot/frame "f"
expect preview /slot/index 0
expect preview /dy -35
expect order f a b c
expect state /history/undoSteps 2
pointer up 30 15
expect clean
expect preview /kind null
expect order f b a c
expect state /history/undoSteps 3
expect state /confirmedSeq 3

# 6. A pan with the middle button: the camera moves, nothing is selected or written, and the history has nothing new.
pointer down 100 100 middle
expect state /pointer/cursor "grabbing"
pointer move 130 90 middle
pointer move 150 120 middle
pointer up 150 120 middle
expect state /camera/x 50
expect state /camera/y 20
expect state /camera/zoom 1
expect state /selection ["b"]
expect state /history/undoSteps 3
expect state /confirmedSeq 3

# 7. A zoom to the pointer: a wheel with Ctrl at the screen point (64, 68), which is the world point (14, 48), just inside the top
# left corner of `a` (now second in `f`, drawn from y 45 to 65). The zoom is e^0.2 (the wheel's rate is 0.01 for each pixel), and the
# world point stays under the pointer: x is 64 - 14 z and y is 68 - 48 z. The same screen point is still over `a`, which a zoom
# about another point would have moved away from.
pointer move 64 68
expect state /pointer/hover "a"
action {"type":"camera","op":{"type":"wheel","wheel":{"dx":0,"dy":-20,"mods":{"ctrl":true}},"at":{"x":64,"y":68}}}
expect state /camera/zoom 1.2214027581601699
expect state /camera/x 46.90036138575762
expect state /camera/y 9.372667608311843
pointer move 64 68
expect state /pointer/hover "a"
expect state /history/undoSteps 3

# 8. Back to the start, one step at a time. The camera is not history, so the zoom stays.
undo
expect order f a b c
expect state /history/undoSteps 2
undo
expect node fg w 30
expect node fg h 30
expect node fg x 30
expect state /history/undoSteps 1
undo
expect node fg x 20
expect node fg y 20
expect state /history/undoSteps 0
expect state /history/canUndo false
expect state /history/canRedo true
expect state /camera/zoom 1.2214027581601699
# Three edits and three undos, all confirmed by the made-up server.
expect state /confirmedSeq 6
expect state /pending []
